msgctxt "64"
msgid "Ah, here y'are! Let's see what ya brought me..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "112"
msgid ""
"Ah, a goya. This one looks nice n' fresh, with healthy\r\n"
"colorin'."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "124"
msgid "You handed over a <Color:8>Bitter Melon<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "136"
msgid "Woo-hoo! So \"goya\" really does mean \"bitter melon\"!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "160"
msgid ""
"Found some dugwai, did ya? This is the source of vitality\r\n"
"in my juice."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "172"
msgid "You gave her some <Color:8>Aloe<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "184"
msgid "So \"dugwai\" means \"aloe\"!? I never knew that."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "208"
msgid ""
"Aha, some kuruzata. This should be sweet and delicious⑬\r\n"
"much better than white sugar when it comes to makin' juice."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "220"
msgid "You gave her some <Color:8>Brown Sugar<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "232"
msgid "Wow, so \"kuruzata\" must mean \"brown sugar.\" That's a toughie."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "256"
msgid ""
"Ooh! You found some shikwasa! These're more sour than\r\n"
"lemons, and perfect for my juice! I'll bet it cost a\r\n"
"fortune, though."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "268"
msgid "You gave her some <Color:8>Shikwasa<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "292"
msgid ""
"Shikwasa works better than lemons? She should've told us\r\n"
"that in the first place..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "316"
msgid ""
"Well, look at this. Some nice-lookin' basanai. And island\r\n"
"basanai, at that! These must've cost a pretty penny. But\r\n"
"I bet they'll be much more tasty."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "328"
msgid "You gave her some <Color:8>Island Bananas<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "352"
msgid ""
"So island bananas are more expensive and taste better than\r\n"
"the normal ones? Wow, thanks, mister!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "376"
msgid ""
"This is a fine lemon indeed. I'll need it to soften the\r\n"
"bitter melon flavor."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "388"
msgid "You gave her a <Color:8>Lemon<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "400"
msgid "At least \"lemon\" still means \"lemon.\" That's an easy one."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "424"
msgid ""
"Well, look at this. Some nice-lookin' basanai. Sweet n'\r\n"
"delicious, I'm sure."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "436"
msgid "You gave her some <Color:8>Bananas<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "448"
msgid "So \"basanai\" means \"bananas\"? I can kinda see that."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "484"
msgid ""
"So, y'brought all the ingredients? Good, now I can whip ya\r\n"
"up a nice batch of goya juice. Don't ya worry 'bout a thing!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "496"
msgid "Really!? Thank you so much!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "568"
msgid "Here y'are. One fresh serving of goya juice, made just for you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "580"
msgid "Wow... So the Mythical Goya Juice... It was real after all!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "592"
msgid ""
"The basanai and dugwai are very important ingredients, too,\r\n"
"y'know. Don't forget that."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "604"
msgid ""
"I'm gonna take this right to my mom! Thanks so much, ma'am!\r\n"
"And you, too, mister!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "628"
msgid ""
"That was really kind of you. I'm sure that juice will help\r\n"
"the kid's mom get better."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "640"
msgid ""
"Well, aren't you the kindest fella? Honestly, it felt right\r\n"
"proper makin' a big batch of goya juice after all this time."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "652"
msgid ""
"Folks reckon my juice packs some mythical, medicinal punch\r\n"
"that'll cure any sickness. But to tell the truth, there's\r\n"
"nothin' real mysterious about it no more."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "664"
msgid ""
"Y'see, back in my day, basanai, lemons, n' dugwai were so\r\n"
"darn expensive, almost no one could afford 'em."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "676"
msgid ""
"Just so happened our goya juice was the healthiest thing around. But these "
"days, nearly anyone can get their hands on those ingredients."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "688"
msgid ""
"Well, to that kid, I'm sure it's still the mythical remedy\r\n"
"his mom needed. Nothing could've been better."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "700"
msgid ""
"Even though you stopped making it years ago, a lot of people\r\n"
"are still talking about it. That alone tells me it's some\r\n"
"incredible stuff."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "712"
msgid ""
"Thank ya for liftin' an old woman's spirits. Now I gave\r\n"
"all the juice to that boy, but this'll also fix ya up right\r\n"
"quick."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "724"
msgid "You got a <Color:8>Staminan Spark<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "748"
msgid "Thank you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "772"
msgid "You got a <Color:8>Staminan Royale<Color:Default>."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "796"
msgid "Thank you."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "808"
msgid "Goodbye, n' good luck to ya."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "880"
msgid "You got 3,000 EXP."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "892"
msgid ""
"This isn't enough for me to make a full batch of goya juice.\r\n"
"Ya gotta bring me more ingredients."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "904"
msgid ""
"(It would help if I knew what to bring... Well, back to the\r\n"
"Public Market, I suppose.)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "940"
msgid ""
"Goya is the most important ingredient in my juice.\r\n"
"We can't get anywhere without that."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "952"
msgid ""
"I know \"goya\" means \"bitter melon.\" They should be selling\r\n"
"them at the Public Market."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "976"
msgid ""
"They should be sellin' dugwai over there... It's a thorny\r\n"
"plant, good for soothin' burns."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1000"
msgid "I'm sure they must be sellin' kuruzata over there..."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1012"
msgid ""
"\"Kuruzata\"? I wonder what that is? I think the \"zata\" part\r\n"
"might mean \"sugar.\""
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1036"
msgid "A lemon's a lemon, plain n' simple. Gotta be nice n' sour."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "1060"
msgid ""
"Basanai, silly. Y'know how it's yellow and sweet?\r\n"
"...Don't young folks say \"basanai\" anymore?"
msgstr ""

